Subject: [PATCH 3] bpf: derive and use exact array-element capabilities

Base: patches 0001 and 0002 on the pinned Leaf RFC.

Retain semantic use markers as well as lookup identity. A sealed executive
gateway derives a child from the map-owned parent, checks element alignment,
and returns only the child. Its map context and saved capability registers
stay on the non-vmapped executive stack, outside Leaf's vmalloc RDDC.

Emit capability copies, constant offsets, and capability-base value accesses.
Require exact representability for every element; inherit parent permissions.
Refuse unsupported metadata, rewrites, and execution paths, including
interpreter fallback. Scope: one ordinary mmapable ARRAY, SOCKET_FILTER,
forward branches, no pointer spills, remaining helpers, atomics, subprograms
or constant blinding. The existing broad Leaf RDDC is not removed.

This is a positive execution demonstration, not a complete compartment
isolation claim or a negative-access evaluation.

---
